{
  "email": "dana.whitfield@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Identify ticket sender, department and title for software request"
}

{
  "query": "PDF editor Company Portal approved software",
  "reason": "Check whether an approved PDF editor is available in Company Portal"
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Dana, thanks for checking with us before installing anything. We can't install software from a download link that came in an email, even from a vendor you know. Free installers from outside sites are a common way for malware to get in. Please don't download or run that file. One important question first: have you already clicked the link, downloaded the file or run it? If you have, please reply right away so we can check your laptop. To get you a PDF editor safely: 1) Open the Company Portal (Software Center) on your laptop and search for \"PDF\". If an approved PDF editor is listed, you can install it yourself without waiting for IT. 2) If nothing there does what you need, reply and tell us what you need to do with PDFs (for example edit text, fill in and sign forms, or combine files) and why you need it for work. We'll then send an approved PDF editor through a security review and the normal approval process. Thanks!",
  "internal_note": "Requester: Dana Whitfield, CEO (Executive), VIP, user_id 1, device BL-LT-0101. She asked IT to install a 'free PDF editor' from a link a vendor sent her: http://free-pdf-tools.example/setup.exe. Following KB-027, I declined the install. IT doesn't install software from links received by email, and any app not in the Company Portal needs approval and a security review. I sent her to the Company Portal for an approved PDF app and asked for her requirements and business reason. I also asked whether she has already clicked, downloaded or run the file. If yes, treat it as a possible compromise (KB-029 path) and escalate right away. A vendor emailing a direct .exe link to the CEO could be a phishing/whaling attempt. If she confirms it came by email and looks suspicious, escalate to security under KB-008 with the sender and subject so the sender can be reviewed and blocked. No actions taken. Nothing escalated yet, because KB-027's escalation condition (app not in the Portal and approval in place) isn't met.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-027",
    "KB-008"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
